The APU board exists in two revisions 1C and 1D, with two memory setups 2GB or 4GB:

  * APU 1C: 3 LAN / 2 GB DRAM / T40E CPU (deprecated)
  * APU 1C4, 3 LAN / 4 GB DRAM / T40E CPU  (deprecated)
  * APU 1D,  3 LAN / 2 GB DRAM / T40E CPU
  * APU 1D4,  3 LAN / 4 GB DRAM / T40E CPU 

Changes between 1C and 1D revisions are minor. Revision 1D features : a better SATA header power, a more stable LAN support and corrects minors issues.

All boards feature:

   * CPU: AMD G series T40E, 1 GHz dual Bobcat core with 64 bit support, 32K data + 32K instruction + 512K L2 cache per core.
   * DRAM: 2 or 4 GB DDR3-1066 DRAM. Soldered on board.
   * Storage: Boot from SD card (connected through USB), external USB or m-SATA SSD. 1 SATA + power connector.
   * 12V DC, about 6 to 12W depending on CPU load. Jack = 2.5 mm, center positive.
   * Connectivity: 3 Gigabit Ethernet channels (Realtek RTL8111E).
   * I/O: DB9 serial port, 2 USB external + 2 internal, three front panel LEDs, pushbutton.
   * Expansion: 2 miniPCI express (one with SIM socket), LPC bus, GPIO header, I2C bus, COM2 (3.3V RXD / TXD).
   * Board size: 6 x 6" (152.4 x 152.4 mm) - same as ALIX.2D13 and WRAP.1E.
   * Firmware: CoreBoot (please contact support@pcengines.ch for source code if desired).
   * Cooling: Conductive cooling from the CPU and south bridge to the enclosure using a 3 mm alu heat spreader (included).

AC/DC is 12v. Previous PC Engines boards were 18v. If you plug the APU to a 18v AC/DC, it will fry. Only use 12v AC/DC.

==== Kernel modules =====
The following kernel modules are needed:
  * Realtek RTL8111/8168B PCI Express Gigabit Ethernet : r8169
  * Intel i2c: i2c_core + i2c_piix4
  * USB: usbcore + usb_storage 
  * SATA support: libata, libahci,ahci
  * SP5100 TCO Timer/Watchdog (allowing waking up): sp5100_tco 
  * LPC bus: Is used for recovery using BIOS plug. Could it be used for parallel port. Driver?
  * GPIO headers: ?
  * Push button: ?
  * Mini PCI-Express: ?
  * ACPI: ?

